{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And their dominion is lost.</b> Their kingdom." "<b>Heshbon is lost, unto Dibon —</b> the kingdom and yoke that Moab had in Heshbon was lost from there, and likewise unto Dibon. The Targum renders סָר as 'עַד' — that is, סַר נִיר מִדִּיבֹן ('the yoke departed from Dibon'). נִיר is a term of kingdom and yoke of a ruler's dominion, as in ״לְמַעַן הֱיוֹת נִיר לְדָוִד עַבְדִּי״ (1 Kings 11)." "<b>And we laid waste.</b> Shin with dagesh — a term of desolation. Thus the parable-makers say: ״וַנַּשִּׁים אוֹתָם עַד נֹפַח״ — we desolated them unto Nophah."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:06.194488636Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}